#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166640 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76054a-1e1c-5091-bd52-39d12fe4e5d8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/id #uuid "41c8053f-0ad2-5b59-ba77-8f4fda1db022" :question/math-academy-id "e-8440" :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle \\int 4\\sinh 2x \\cosh 2x \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta}=2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the double-angle formula for the hyperbolic sine:\n\n$$\n\\sinh {2\\theta} =2\\sinh \\theta \\cosh \\theta\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta= 2x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\sinh {4x} =2\\sinh 2x \\cosh 2x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sinh {4x}= \\sinh 2x \\cosh 2x\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int4\\sinh 2x\\cosh 2xdx &= \\int4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sinh 4xdx \\\\\n&= \\int2\\sinh 4xdx \\\\\n&= 2\\int\\sinh 4xdx \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cosh 4x + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\cosh 4x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166641 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "425eb518-c5c6-5815-adf2-a54350f59d4d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/id #uuid "b6c11fbd-00db-5506-baf0-2b6a94bfa6e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-8441" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\cosh^2{x} + \\sinh^2{x}\\ \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x}= \\cos^2{x}-\\sin^2{x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cosh 2x = \\cosh^2{x} + \\sinh^2{x}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\cosh^{2} x + \\sinh^{2} xdx &= \\int\\cosh 2xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sinh 2x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166642 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e604fdb1-483e-54fb-b6ab-53912c968506" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Squared Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "c91d7451-c9b5-57a1-9284-ec3fb617220c" :question/math-academy-id "e-8442" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 2\\cosh^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cosh{2x} =2\\cosh^2 x -1\n$$\n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cosh 2x +1 \\right)\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int2\\cosh^{2} xdx &= \\int2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\cosh 2x + 1)dx \\\\\n&= \\int(\\cosh 2x + 1)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sinh 2x + x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166643 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d245094e-5e59-5dd9-85c1-9f0b5ca764e3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Squared Sine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "5d3a47d6-5a07-5fb6-9f57-23e74a7ba24f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8443" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2} 8\\sinh^2{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos {2x}=1-2\\sin^2x\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cosh{2x} = 1+ 2\\sinh^2{x}\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\sinh^2x = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\cosh {2x} -1\\right)\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\ln 2}8\\sinh^{2} xdx &= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2}8 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\cosh 2x - 1)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2}4\\cosh 2x - 4dx \\\\\n&= \\left.(2\\sinh 2x - 4x)\\right|_{0}^{\\ln 2} \\\\\n&= (2\\sinh (2\\ln 2) - 4\\ln 2) - (2\\sinh 0 - 4 \\cdot 0) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\frac{e^{2\\ln 2} - e^{-2\\ln 2}}{2} - 4\\ln 2 \\\\\n&= (2^{2} - 2^{-2}) - 4\\ln 2 \\\\\n&= \\frac{15}{4} - 4\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76054a-1e1c-5091-bd52-39d12fe4e5d8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d77b2b55-608b-516a-93e0-fecefa5871d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\cosh 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165705} {:answer/id #uuid "f04658dc-e4b3-5bf9-868a-523601c3dc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\sinh 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165706} {:answer/id #uuid "53a82082-34d9-5935-a953-63a01f7ac0d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\cosh 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165707} {:answer/id #uuid "62578e34-5db8-575c-846b-2c94df369549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\sinh 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165708} {:answer/id #uuid "71678e1c-b9b6-5857-9ac6-46bb87857610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cosh 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165709}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d29f9933-7887-5a5d-9783-38c6cd697ae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :